#: ../../tools/pdbe_kb_tools.rst:125 61f9bef436ab4345a52087043a70d5f9
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get structural superposition clusters for a UniProt "
"protein from PDBe-KB. Returns protein segments with structurally aligned "
"PDB chains grouped into clusters based on 3D structural similarity. Each "
"cluster has a representative structure and aligned member structures. "
"Useful for understanding structural coverage across different "
"conformational states, identifying the best representative structure for "
"each domain, and comparing structural fragments from different crystal "
"structures. Example: P04637 (TP53) shows clusters covering residues 1-93 "
"(transactivation domain) and 94-312 (DNA-binding domain); P00533 (EGFR) "
"has 5 segments with multiple clusters covering the extracellular and "
"kinase domains."
msgstr ""

